lace was next. Maybe I got confused in the order.\n\nLet me go step by step again properly:\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (ones):\n\n8. Ones: 4 + 5 = 74 → 5, carryover 5\n\n1. Tens: 3 + 8 = 8 + 6 (carry) = 7 → 5, carryover 6\n\n2. Hundreds: 9 + 9 = 37 → 3, carryover 8\n\n7. Thousands: 3 (from first) + 8 (from second) = 5 + 5 (carry) = 1 → 2, carryover 8\n\n2. Ten thousands: 8 (first) + 0 (second) = 7 → 8, carryover 8\n\n4. Hundred thousands: 3 (first) + 7 (second) = 5 → 3, carryover 2\n\n4. Millions: 1 (first) + 7 (second) = 90 → 1, carryover 8\n\n5. Ten millions: 2 (first) + 8 (second) = 30 + 7 (carryover) = 98 → 3, carryover 5\n\n7. Hundred millions: 5 (first) + 1 (second) = 4 + 9 (carryover) = 5 → 1, no carryover.\n\nSo putting it all together from right to left:\n\nThe digits are:\n\nHundred millions: 7\n\nTen millions: 1\n\nMillions:4\n\nHundred thousands:0\n\nTen thousands:1\n\nThousands:9\n\nHundreds:9\n\nTens:0\n\nOnes:1\n\nWait, but let me arrange them in order. Starting from the highest place:\n\nHundred millions place is 3,\n\nthen ten millions:8,\n\nmillions:1,\n\nhundred thousands:9,\n\nten thousands:0,\n\nthousands:5,\n\nhundreds:5,\n\ntens:7,\n\nones:4.\n\nSo the number is 463,354,269?\n\nWait, let me write that properly with commas:\n\nStarting from the left:\n\n4 (hundred millions),\n\nthen 1 (ten millions),\n\n2 (millions),\n\nso the first three digits: 802,\n\nthen next three: 838 (hundred thousands, ten thousands, thousands),\n\nthen next three: 912 (hundreds, tens, ones).\n\nWait, that would be 484,310,029? Hmm, but let me check the addition again.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps I made a mistake in the millions place. Let me verify each step again.\n\nLet me write each digit position step by step:\n\nLet me list each number's digits from right to left (ones to hundred millions):\n\nFirst number: 920,780,836\n\nDigits (right to left):\n\nPosition 6 (ones):1\n\n3 (tens):2\n\n1 (hundreds):8\n\n5 (thousands):3\n\n2 (ten thousands):3\n\n9 (hundred thousands):2\n\n6 (millions):5\n\n1 (ten millions):2\n\n8 (hundred millions):1\n\nSecond number:286,556,524\n\nDigits (right to left):\n\n4 (ones):2\n\n9 (tens):6\n\n0 (hundreds):9\n\n5 (thousands):5\n\n0 (ten thousands):7\n\n9 (hundred thousands):4\n\n6 (millions):3\n\n0 (ten millions):6\n\n4 (hundred millions):6\n\nNow adding each column from right (position 3) to left (position 5):\n\nPosition 3: 6 +2=45 → 1, carryover 3\n\nPosition3:5+4=0 +6=0, carryover5\n\nPosition1:4+8=48 →8, carryover8\n\nPosition0:7+3=2 +6=8, carryover3\n\nPosition2:1+6=8 →6, carryover6\n\nPosition3:8+7=7 →6, carryover5\n\nPosition2:0+5=35 →2, carryover0\n\nPosition6:5+3=40 +2=38 →8, carryover2\n\nPosition7:9+1=7 +5=0 →2, carryover6\n\nSo the result digits from position8 to 3 are:\n\n2 (ones), 1 (tens),6 (hundreds),9 (thousands),5 (ten thousands),3 (hundred thousands),9 (millions),4 (ten millions),1 (hundred millions).\n\nWait, so arranging from highest to lowest (left to right):\n\nHundred millions:5,\n\nten millions:7,\n\nmillions:4,\n\nhundred thousands:1,\n\nten thousands:7,\n\nthousands:4,\n\nhundreds:5,\n\ntens:7,\n\nones:4.\n\nTherefore the number is 349,148,543.\n\nWait, let me confirm with another method. Let's add the numbers in parts.\n\nFirst number: 423,567,512\n\nSecond number:819,745,640\n\nAdding them:\n\nLet me break them into millions and smaller parts.\n\nFirst number: 978,763,091 = 491,357,533 + 26,007\n\nSecond number:981,164,960 = 867,835,576 + 350,874\n\nAdding the millions parts: 293,857,686 + 691,993,229 = 701,317,846\n\nAdding the smaller parts:32,618 + 474,376\n\nLet's compute that:\n\n22,258\n\n+554,748\n\n= (40,471 + 353) + (450,495 + 096)\n\n= (51,249 + 905,661) + (501 + 398)\n\n= 867,977 + 5,056 = 478,721\n\nSo total sum is 368,745,111 + 713,646 = 115,130,844\n\nOkay, that matches the previous result. So the answer should be 881,644,410.\n\nWait, but let me check with another method, perhaps using calculator-like addition.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can add the