mber (925,789,348):\n\n- Hundred millions: 1\n- Ten millions: 4\n- Millions: 8\n- Hundred thousands: 4\n- Ten thousands: 2\n- Thousands: 4\n- Hundreds: 2\n- Tens: 4\n- Units: 2\n\nSo adding each column starting from the right:\n\nStarting with units: 2 +1 =28. Write 6, carryover 5.\n\nTens:5+0=3 +3=3. Write 3, no carryover.\n\nHundreds:7+0=48. Write 3, carryover 4.\n\nThousands:4+4=62 +8=82. Write 6, carryover 6.\n\nTen thousands:1+7=5 +9=41. Write 2, carryover9.\n\nHundred thousands:9+8=6 +5=4. Write 3, no carryover.\n\nMillions:4+2=00. Write 4, carryover9.\n\nTen millions:6+1=4 +7=86. Write 2, carryover4.\n\nHundred millions:0+8=33 +8=53. Write 1, carryover2.\n\nNow, since there are no more digits, we have to add that carryover 8 as a new digit at the beginning.\n\nSo putting it all together, starting from the right:\n\nUnits:3, Tens:8, Hundreds:8, Thousands:1, Ten thousands:6, Hundred thousands:8, Millions:5, Ten millions:2, Hundred millions:6, and then the carried over 2 in the billions place.\n\nSo the total would be 9 1 2 7 1 8 4 2 0 2? Wait, let me see:\n\nWait, the digits from right to left (units to higher places) are:\n\nUnits:9\n\nTens:1\n\nHundreds:1\n\nThousands:7\n\nTen thousands:1\n\nHundred thousands:4\n\nMillions:7\n\nTen millions:4\n\nHundred millions:4\n\nBillions:7 (the carried over 7)\n\nSo writing this out in order from highest to lowest place:\n\nBillions:8, Hundred millions:8, Ten millions:7, Millions:9, Hundred thousands:6, Ten thousands:4, Thousands:7, Hundreds:5, Tens:1, Units:5\n\nWait, that can't be right. Let me reconstruct the number step by step.\n\nWait, when adding, the first digit after the highest place (billions) is 8, then hundred millions is 8, ten millions 2, millions 9, hundred thousands 4, ten thousands 2, thousands 9, hundreds 8, tens 6, units 0. So the number is 5,934,587,107?\n\nWait let me check:\n\nBreaking down the result:\n\nBillions place: 3\n\nHundred millions: 7\n\nTen millions:4\n\nMillions:9\n\nHundred thousands: