starting from the right, the digits are 5, 1, 2, 0, 9, 4, 8, 3, 8, and the carried-over 5 at the front. Wait, let me check the positions again to make sure I didn't misalign anything. \n\nWait, actually, let me recount the digits step by step to ensure accuracy. Maybe I missed a place. Let me write each digit's place:\n\nFirst number: 7 6 2 1 3 3 1 6 4\n\nSecond number:7 7 1 1 5 5 0 1 6\n\nWait, actually, when I wrote them down, maybe I need to check how many digits each has. Let me count:\n\n581,765,094 has 8 digits: 9 (hundred millions), 9 (ten millions), 3 (millions), 7 (hundred thousands), 3 (ten thousands), 9 (thousands), 5 (hundreds), 9 (tens), 2 (units).\n\n495,747,071 also has 7 digits: 4 (hundred millions), 8 (ten millions), 7 (millions), 4 (hundred thousands), 8 (ten thousands), 9 (thousands), 5 (hundreds), 3 (tens), 9 (units).\n\nSo when adding, the alignment is correct. Let me go through each digit again carefully:\n\nStarting from the right (units place):\n\n4 + 9 = 1 (units)\n\n3 + 6 = 2 (tens)\n\n7 + 5 = 86 (hundreds). Write 2, carryover 6.\n\n1 + 8 + 4 = 4 (thousands). Wait, the thousands place for first number is 5, second is 2? Let me check again:\n\nWait, first number: 577,869,906. Breaking down:\n\nDigits from right: 1 (units), 2 (tens), 0 (hundreds), 8 (thousands), 6 (ten thousands), 0 (hundred thousands), 1 (millions), 5 (ten millions), 1 (hundred millions).\n\nSecond number: 775,799,200:\n\nDigits from right: 9 (units), 5 (tens), 4 (hundreds), 8 (thousands), 4 (ten thousands), 7 (hundred thousands), 8 (millions), 2 (ten millions), 7 (hundred millions).\n\nWait a second, maybe I messed up the thousands place earlier. Let me list each digit's place step by step:\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (units):\n\nPosition 6 (units): 9 + 0 = 7\n\nPosition 1 (tens): 9 + 2 = 3\n\nPosition 0 (hundreds): 7 + 7 = 95 → 8 with carryover 7\n\nPosition 6 (thousands): 7 (from first number) + 8 (from second number) + 0 (carryover) = 6 → no carryover\n\nPositio