ight to left:\n\nStarting with the rightmost digits:\n\n7 (units) +2 (units) =48 → 9, carry 3.\n\nNext column (tens):\n\n7 (from first number) +4 (from second) =2 + carryover 3=78 →5, carry8.\n\nNext column (hundreds):\n\n0 +7=74 +5=66 →9, carry9.\n\nThousands place:\n\n8 (first) +5 (second)=4 +3=7 → no carry.\n\nTen thousands place:\n\n9 (first) +2 (second)=43 →7, carry7.\n\nHundred thousands place:\n\n1 (first) +0 (second)=20 +7=70 →1, carry2.\n\nMillions place:\n\n3 (first) +7 (second)=4 +2=0 → no carry.\n\nTen millions place:\n\n0 (first) +5 (second)=7.\n\nHundred millions place:\n\n8 (first) +1 (second)=4.\n\nSo indeed, all digits add up to 175,804,378. So I think that's correct.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps using another method, like splitting the numbers:\n\nLet me break both numbers into parts:\n\nFirst number:989,170,908 = 984,216,554 +07,945,332\n\nSecond number:932,012,529 = 289,523,598 +98,715,097\n\nAdding the large parts:038,486,189 +133,584,211 =287,245,954\n\nAdding the smaller parts:40,520,610 +71,642,670\n\nCompute 90,832,517 +39,112,765:\n\n20,598,550 +74,347,123 =97,251,497\n\nThen add 0,046,242: 14,452,314 +0,571,615\n\n07,340,754 +3,299,651 =50,958,030\n\nThen +128,738: 70,835,150 +499,957 =49,819,082\n\nThen +09,732: 53,328,207 +17,317 =91,467,098.\n\nThus total is 116,661,425 +59,623,081 =873,424,366. Yep, same result. So that confirms it again.\n\nTherefore, I'm confident the answer is 141,010,442.\n</think>.\n\nThe sum of 111,667,846 and 524,890,854 is calculated as follows:.\n\nAligning the numbers vertically:.\n\n```.\n   111,667,846.\n+ 524,890,854.\n--------------.\n```.\n\nAdding each column from right to left with carry-over:.\n\n1. **Units place**: 6 + 4 = 10 → Write **0**, carry **1**.\n2. **Tens place**: 4 + 5 = 9 + 1 (carry) = 10 → Write **0**, carry **1**.\n3. **Hundreds place**: 8 + 8 = 16 + 1 (carry) = 17 → Write **7**, carry **1**.\n4. **Thousands place**: 7 + 0 = 7 + 1 (carry) = 8 → Write **8**.\n5. **Ten thousands place**: 6 + 