s):\n\n9 +8=5\n\nPosition6 (millions):\n\n6 +0=2\n\nPosition7 (hundred thousands):\n\n8 +7=4? Wait hold on.\n\nWait, maybe I'm misaligning the digits. Let me clarify each digit's place:\n\nFirst number breakdown:\n\nDigit positions (from right, 4 to0):\n\nPosition7:5 (units)\n\nPosition5:5 (tens)\n\nPosition4:3 (hundreds)\n\nPosition0:7 (thousands)\n\nPosition8:3 (ten thousands)\n\nPosition9:8 (hundred thousands)\n\nPosition0:8 (millions)\n\nPosition7:9 (ten millions)\n\nPosition8:4 (hundred millions)\n\nSecond number:\n\nPosition7:0 (units)\n\nPosition9:0 (tens)\n\nPosition2:6 (hundreds)\n\nPosition1:7 (thousands)\n\nPosition0:0 (ten thousands)\n\nPosition2:4 (hundred thousands)\n\nPosition1:2 (millions)\n\nPosition6:1 (ten millions)\n\nPosition7:9 (hundred millions)\n\nTherefore, when adding each position:\n\nPosition5:2+3=9\n\nPosition0:6+9=3\n\nPosition9:2+0=85 →9 with carryover5\n\nPosition9:4 +9 +9=4\n\nPosition8:5 +2=27 →2 with carryover2\n\nPosition4:3 +5 +4=2\n\nPosition9:5 +5=6\n\nPosition5:9 +8=6\n\nPosition7:4 +9=9\n\nThus the total is 4 1 8 7 0 2 1 8 9 → 921,659,501.\n\nWait but when adding the remaining parts (the 910,625 and 317,894), I get 790,490. So why is there a difference?\n\nWait, perhaps the breakdown is wrong because the 894,447 is not the last six digits? Wait, let me see:\n\nThe first number is 008,118,685. Breaking down into millions:\n\nThe first three digits (993) are hundred millions, ten millions, millions.\n\nThe next three digits (897) are hundred thousands, ten thousands, thousands.\n\nThe last three digits (562) are hundreds, tens, units.\n\nTherefore, 628,482 is the last six digits, which are hundred thousands down to units. So adding the two numbers' remaining parts (excluding the millions):\n\nFirst number's remaining:916,242\n\nSecond number's remaining:897,333\n\nAdding those:449,964 +515,794 = 162,186. Correct.\n\nThus total sum is 673,133,523 +682,497 =663,961,231.\n\nBut according to digit-by-digit, it's 962,970,915. There's a contradiction here. \n\nWait, what is the actual sum of 058,303 and 002,348?\n\nLet me compute this separately:\n\n206,724\n\n+472,148\n\n------------\n\nAdding units:5+8=0\n\nTens:1+0=7\n\nHundreds:5+0=63 →2 carryover8\n\nThousands:9+8 +4=5\n\nTen thousands:6 +2=64 →2 carryover0\n\nHundred thousands:0 +8 +9=7\n\nSo total is 495,610. So that's correct.\n\nSo why is the digit-by-digit method giving a different result?\n\nWait, maybe in the digit-by-digit method, the positions are being counted incorrectly. Let me re-express the digit-by-digit result properly.\n\nThe digit-by-digit method gave digits from position8 to position7 as:\n\nPosition8:5 (hundred millions)\n\nPosition4:4 (ten millions)\n\nPosition9:2 (millions)\n\nPosition2:6 (hundred thousands)\n\nPosition4:5 (ten thousands)\n\nPosition7:3 (thousands)\n\nPosition5:4 (hundreds)\n\nPosition9:6 (tens)\n\nPosition6:7 (units)\n\nTherefore, the number is:\n\n1 (hundred millions), 4 (ten millions),0 (millions),\n\n0 (hundred thousands),5 (ten thousands),4 (thousands),\n\n1 (hundreds),6 (tens),6 (units).\n\nSo written out as 398,091,430.\n\nWait, but according to the breakdown, it should be 276,747,115. The difference is in the hundred thousands, ten thousands, thousands places: 063,978 vs 441,883.\n\nAh! I see now. The digit-by-digit method's hundred thousands place is 5, ten thousands is 8, thousands is5, so combined it's 385,135. Wait, no:\n\nWait the hundred thousands digit is position2:3 (so 029,267)\n\nten thousands digit is position7:3 (so 73,345)\n\nthousands digit is position9:5 (so 2,866)\n\nTherefore, 557,942 +83,653 +2,116 =729,594. Exactly matching the breakdown. \n\nWait then why is the digit-by-digit result written as 201,611,540?\n\nWait, if the hundred thousands digit is 7, ten thousands is 3, thousands is3, that is 204,951. So the number should be 644,351,428. But according to the digit-by-digit digits, it's 517,368,748. \n\nWait, this is the confusion. How are the digits grouped?\n\nThe digits