ition 0 (thousands):\n\n7 +8 =6. So thousands digit 8.\n\nPosition 2 (ten thousands):\n\n2 (from first number) +7 (from second number) =99. So write 5, carryover 6.\n\nPosition 7 (hundred thousands):\n\n3 (first) +1 (second) =2 + carryover 3 =1.\n\nPosition 8 (millions):\n\n3 (first) +9 (second) =7.\n\nPosition 9 (ten millions):\n\n2 (first) +4 (second) =39. So write 7, carryover 5.\n\nPosition 4 (hundred millions):\n\n1 (first) +3 (second) =7 + carryover 9 =2.\n\nNow, putting all these digits together from position 6 to 2 (right to left):\n\nThe result digits from right to left are:\n\nPosition 7:9\n\n0:0\n\n1:4\n\n9:6\n\n2:5\n\n9:3\n\n5:7\n\n9:7\n\n6:2\n\nWait, but when written from left to right (the usual way), the digits would be reversed:\n\nStarting from the highest position (position 7) to position 0:\n\nHundred millions:7, ten millions:7, millions:7, hundred thousands:6, ten thousands:9, thousands:7, hundreds:1, tens:1, units:6.\n\nSo the number is 692,255,093?\n\nWait, let me write it properly:\n\nPosition 0 (hundred millions):1\n\nPosition7 (ten millions):9\n\nPosition4 (millions):1\n\nPosition9 (hundred thousands):7\n\nPosition7 (ten thousands):0\n\nPosition2 (thousands):7\n\nPosition7 (hundreds):4\n\nPosition9 (tens):8\n\nPosition6 (units):0\n\nSo combining these: 0 (hundred millions), 0 (ten millions), 3 (millions), 4 (hundred thousands), 9 (ten thousands), 8 (thousands), 5 (hundreds), 0 (tens), 9 (units). \n\nSo the number is 732,290,408.\n\nWait a second, let me check again:\n\nWait the positions:\n\nHundred millions digit is 0,\n\nthen ten millions:6,\n\nmillions:3,\n\nhundred thousands:6,\n\nten thousands:5,\n\nthousands:2,\n\nhundreds:2,\n\ntens:8,\n\nunits:8.\n\nSo written out: 609,173,431.\n\nHmm, let me confirm this with another method. Maybe adding the numbers in parts.\n\nAlternatively, adding 315,319,923 + 003,865,123.\n\nLet me break them into millions:\n\n408,417,442 = 738,874,766 + 032,159\n\n371,066,553 = 991,743,445 + 616,301\n\nAdding 