\n+546,861,563  \n=?\n\nLet me add the numbers digit by digit again:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n2+3 =5  \n9+6=15 (5, carryover 1)  \n8+5=13 +1=14 (4, carryover1)  \n3+1=4 +1=5  \n7+6=13 (3, carryover1)  \n8+8=16 +1=17 (7, carryover1)  \n9+6=15 +1=16 (6, carryover1)  \n6+4=10 +1=11 (1, carryover1)  \n2+5=7 +1=8.  \n\nSo the total is 816,735,455. Therefore, the correct answer is 816,735,455.  \n\nWait, but in my initial thought process I had different numbers like 333,042,328 and 015,189,107. That was a mistake because I misread the original problem. The user's question is about 269873892 and 546861563, which sum to 816,735,455.  \n\n**Final Answer:**  \nThe sum of 269,873,892 and 546,861,563 is \\boxed{816735455}.",
