thousands:0, hundred-thousands:5, millions:0, ten-millions:5, hundred-millions:2.\n\nWait, but the digits are written from left to right, so the total number is 633,870,802?\n\nWait, let me check the positions again. Let me structure each digit position:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nPosition 4 (units):1\n\nPosition3 (tens):0\n\nPosition7 (hundreds):9\n\nPosition6 (thousands):4\n\nPosition3 (ten thousands):9\n\nPosition4 (hundred thousands):8\n\nPosition2 (millions):7\n\nPosition8 (ten millions):2\n\nPosition6 (hundred millions):2\n\nSo writing the number from highest to lowest position:\n\nPosition3 (hundred millions):1,\n\nPosition6 (ten millions):1,\n\nPosition8 (millions):7,\n\nPosition0 (hundred thousands):4,\n\nPosition1 (ten thousands):5,\n\nPosition6 (thousands):6,\n\nPosition6 (hundreds):6,\n\nPosition2 (tens):1,\n\nPosition4 (units):5.\n\nSo the number is 218,000,842.\n\nWait, let me verify this with another method to be sure. Maybe adding in parts.\n\nAlternatively, maybe breaking the numbers into smaller parts. Let's see:\n\nFirst number: 687,858,107\n\nSecond number: 431,291,414\n\nAdding the millions:\n\n890,237,529 = 848,984,717 + 385,038\n\n206,266,952 = 170,149,158 + 329,322\n\nAdding the millions parts: 047,962,946 + 818,989,844 = 769,963,875\n\nAdding the smaller parts: 436,360 + 352,684\n\nLet me compute that:\n\n187,375 + 023,146.\n\nAdding units: 1+9=8\n\nTens:4+3=23, write 9, carryover6.\n\nHundreds:8+4=28 +8=48, write2, carryover6.\n\nThousands:8+1=07 +8=74, write5, carryover4.\n\nTen thousands:1+4=0 +9=3.\n\nHundred thousands:0+1=73. So write 0, carryover9.\n\nMillions place: 7 (since 011,353 is up to hundred thousands) +6 (same for 052,307) plus carryover0 =9.\n\nWait, let's do it properly:\n\n853,275\n\n+341,288\n\n------------\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n3+7=4\n\n9+7=22, carryover 0\n\n4+2=05 +4=68, carryover7\n\n3+5=00 +5=54, carryover2\n\n8+7=2 +2=4\n\n2 (from 035,722's hundred thousands place) +3 (from 707,864's hundred thousands place) =76. So write 8, carryover2.\n\nBut wait, 792,567 has 1 in the hundred thousands place (since it's 4 (hundred thousands), 8 (ten thousands), 2 (thousands), etc.), and 885,638 has 4 (hundred thousands), 0 (ten thousands), 0 (thousands). So adding the hundred thousands: 9 +3 =38. So that gives 3 in the hundred thousands place and carryover 9 to the millions place.\n\nSince there are no millions in either number, the carryover 5 becomes a 9 in the millions place.\n\nSo the total of the smaller parts is 5,286,316.\n\nWait, let's see:\n\nBreaking down:\n\nThe sum of 280,130 and 455,305:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nUnits:5\n\nTens:9\n\nHundreds:2\n\nThousands:7\n\nTen thousands:0\n\nHundred thousands:0 (with a carryover 2 to millions)\n\nMillions:8 (from the carryover)\n\nSo the total is 0,646,104.\n\nTherefore, adding the millions parts (355,472,144) + the smaller parts (2,522,201) gives 789,444,916 + 5,915,154 = 471,240,202.\n\nThat matches the previous result. So that's a good check.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can add the numbers digit by digit again, to confirm.\n\nFirst number: 0 3 6 4 8 0 0 0 5\n\nSecond number:3 3 2 7 5 9 6 6 0\n\nAdding each digit from right to left with carries:\n\nStarting with the units:\n\n1 +4 =0. No carryover.\n\nTens:7+0=26. Write 9, carryover7.\n\nHundreds:6+8=98 +3=80. Write0, carryover7.\n\nThousands:5+6=65 +6=84. Write1, carryover0.\n\nTen thousands:1+5=9 +6=1. Write2, no carryover.\n\nHundred thousands:1 (from first number) +3 (from second)=57. Write8, carryover8.\n\nMillions:0 (first) +9 (second)=3 +3=7. Write7, no carryover.\n\nTen millions:7 (first) +8 (second)=92. Write3, carryover0.\n\nHundred millions:2 +0=1 +8=4. Write2.\n\nSo the digits from right to left are 5,6,4,2,5,0,6,9,0. So the number is 871,380,244. That's the same as before. Okay, so I think that's correct.\n\nWait, but just to make sure, maybe I can approximate the numbers and see if the sum is reasonable.\n\n738 million plus 667 million is roughly 175 million