irst:6, Second:1. 9+9=64. Write9, carryover8.\n\nPosition8 (hundred thousands):\nFirst:6, Second:4. 6+8=5 + carryover5=6. Write2, carryover1.\n\nPosition6 (millions):\nFirst:1, Second:0. 0+3=00. Write4, carryover3.\n\nPosition9 (ten millions):\nFirst:1, Second:4. 0+3=6 + carryover9=7. Write8, carryover7.\n\nPosition5 (hundred millions):\nFirst:0, Second:7. 1+0=59. Write6, carryover6.\n\nNow, since there's a carryover of 2 from the hundred millions place, we need to add a new digit at the billions place: 8.\n\nSo putting all digits together from right to left:\n\nStarting with the units digit we had:\n\n4 (units)\n5 (tens)\n5 (hundreds)\n2 (thousands)\n2 (ten thousands)\n0 (hundred thousands)\n7 (millions)\n5 (ten millions)\n7 (hundred millions)\n8 (billions)\n\nSo the total number is 9,373,384,829? Wait let me check the order.\n\nWait, the digits from the highest to the lowest place:\n\nBillions:9\n\nHundred millions:3\n\nTen millions:8\n\nMillions:3\n\nHundred thousands:2\n\nTen thousands:4\n\nThousands:3\n\nHundreds:5\n\nTens:3\n\nUnits:0\n\nWait, actually, the digits should be arranged as:\n\nBillions digit:0,\n\nthen hundred millions:2,\n\nten millions:4,\n\nmillions:5,\n\nhundred thousands:9,\n\nten thousands:1,\n\nthousands:2,\n\nhundreds:9,\n\ntens:9,\n\nunits:6.\n\nSo combining these:\n\n5 (billions), 3 (hundred millions), 5 (ten millions), 4 (millions), 2 (hundred thousands?), wait, maybe I need to write them in order:\n\nStarting from the highest place (billions):\n\n4 (billions),\n\nthen 8 (hundred millions),\n\nthen 7 (ten millions),\n\nthen 6 (millions),\n\nthen 0 (hundred thousands),\n\n9 (ten thousands),\n\n0 (thousands),\n\n8 (hundreds),\n\n1 (tens),\n\n6 (units).\n\nSo putting commas appropriately:\n\n4,388,157,543.\n\nWait let's see:\n\nBreaking down the number:\n\nBillions: 4,\n\nHundred millions:3,\n\nTen millions:9,\n\nMillions:0,\n\nHundred thousands:8? Wait, no, the hundred thousands place is 3. Wait, maybe I need to write each segment.\n\nWai