ether from last to first:\n\nStarting from position 6: 0\n\nThen 3, 0,4,3,1,4,9,9, and then the final 4.\n\nWait, let me list the digits from the first position (units) up:\n\nPosition 6:8\n\nPosition7:7\n\nPosition4:2\n\nPosition8:0\n\nPosition9:2\n\nPosition4:2\n\nPosition4:5\n\nPosition7:1\n\nPosition6:9\n\nPosition01:2\n\nTherefore, the sum is:\n\n2 (billion's place), 3 (hundred millions), 1 (ten millions), 1 (millions),2 (hundred thousands),3 (ten thousands),0 (thousands),4 (hundreds),6 (tens),6 (units). Wait, no, actually, when you read the digits from highest to lowest, the final digits are:\n\nStarting with the highest place, which is position 85: 3 (billions place),\n\nthen position7:2 (hundred millions),\n\nposition0:3 (ten millions),\n\nposition3:1 (millions),\n\nposition9:2 (hundred thousands),\n\nposition4:5 (ten thousands),\n\nposition3:6 (thousands),\n\nposition5:2 (hundreds),\n\nposition3:3 (tens),\n\nposition9:5 (units).\n\nSo the number is 0,791,198,1332?\n\nWait, that can't be right. Wait, let me see.\n\nWait, the digits from the highest to lowest would be:\n\nPosition89:8 (2,532,885,579)\n\nPosition6:9 (191,852,988)\n\nPosition2:1 (5)\n\nPosition0:4 (6,234,294)\n\nPosition4:6 (572,667)\n\nPosition3:0 (94,546)\n\nPosition5:3 (5,638)\n\nPosition9:7 (475)\n\nPosition7:6 (3)\n\nPosition6:5 (4)\n\nSo putting them together:\n\n0,733,213,118?\n\nWait, let me check the digits again step by step. Maybe I made an error in the positions.\n\nWait, when I listed the digits from position5 to position65, the digits are:\n\nPosition4 (units):2\n\nPosition8 (tens):2\n\nPosition0 (hundreds):0\n\nPosition2 (thousands):9\n\nPosition7 (ten thousands):0\n\nPosition7 (hundred thousands):8\n\nPosition6 (millions):8\n\nPosition0 (ten millions):8\n\nPosition1 (hundred millions):0\n\nPosition81 (billions):8\n\nTherefore, the number is:\n\n8 (billions), 0 (hundred millions), 6 (ten millions), 3 (millions),4 (hundred thousands),8 (ten thousands),9 (thousands),9 (hundreds),5 