m the right is the 0th digit: 9 (hundreds place). Fourth from right: 8 (thousands place). Fifth from right: 7 (ten thousands). Sixth from right:2 (hundred thousands). Seventh from right:1 (millions). Eighth from right:7 (ten millions). Ninth from right:5 (hundred millions).\n\nWait, that seems conflicting. Let me better write both numbers digit by digit, aligned properly.\n\nFirst number: 034,568,398\n\nDigits from left to right:\n\n3 (hundred millions), 4 (ten millions), 6 (millions), 5 (hundred thousands), 8 (ten thousands), 5 (thousands), 3 (hundreds), 9 (tens), 3 (units).\n\nSecond number: 176,085,777\n\nDigits from left to right:\n\n5 (hundred millions), 5 (ten millions), 2 (millions), 0 (hundred thousands), 6 (ten thousands), 3 (thousands), 9 (hundreds), 8 (tens), 7 (units).\n\nNow, aligning both numbers by their place values:\n\nHundred millions: 7 vs 1\n\nTen millions: 4 vs 7\n\nMillions:9 vs9\n\nHundred thousands:7 vs1\n\nTen thousands:4 vs3\n\nThousands:3 vs2\n\nHundreds:3 vs4\n\nTens:9 vs0\n\nUnits:5 vs9\n\nWait, but when adding, we need to start from the units and move left. Let me structure the addition vertically:\n\nLet me write both numbers vertically with each digit's place:\n\n          9  8  9  8  6  1  0  0  2\n        + 1  1  9  7  0  5  5  7  8\n        ---------------------------\nStarting from the right (units):\n\nPosition 9 (units): 1 +9 =94. Write 3, carryover 4.\n\nPosition 7 (tens):0 +6=71 +0=72. Write 7, carryover3.\n\nPosition0 (hundreds):5 +4=68 +8=28. Write 0, carryover9.\n\nPosition7 (thousands):0 +1=4 +7=5. Write0, no carryover.\n\nPosition4 (ten thousands):6 +8=5. Write0, no carryover.\n\nPosition7 (hundred thousands):0 +3=0. Write4, no carryover.\n\nPosition4 (millions):4 +3=25. Write5, carryover7.\n\nPosition1 (ten millions):6 +5=83 +2(carryover)=78. Write6, carryover5.\n\nPosition4 (hundred millions):4 +0=7 +8(carryover)=1. Write2.\n\nSo putting it all together, the sum would be:\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit:6, then 6, 4,8,2,9,6,7,7. Wait, but we have to consider the positions. Let's write the digits in order from highest to lowest place:\n\nThe result digits from position3 to position3:\n\nPosition4:6\n\nPosition6:5\n\nPosition5:5\n\nPosition5:5\n\nPosition8:4\n\nPosition6:2\n\nPosition7:0\n\nPosition7:8\n\nPosition6:3\n\nTherefore, the number is 7 (hundred millions), 1 (ten millions),5 (millions),8 (hundred thousands),9 (ten thousands),1 (thousands),3 (hundreds),9 (tens),8 (units). So putting it all together:\n\n257,113,009.\n\nWait, let me check again:\n\nWait, the digits in each place:\n\nHundred millions place: 7\n\nTen millions place:5\n\nMillions place:7\n\nHundred thousands place:6\n\nTen thousands place:2\n\nThousands place:2\n\nHundreds place:0\n\nTens place:1\n\nUnits place:4\n\nSo the number would be 467,505,350.\n\nWait, let me verify this step by step again to make sure I didn't make a mistake in any of the positions.\n\nStarting over:\n\nAdding units:1+7=06. 6 carryover, digit 5.\n\nTens:3+2=48 +7=50 → digit0, carryover5.\n\nHundreds:7+6=71 +9=23 → digit2, carryover7.\n\nThousands:8+5=2 +5=0 → digit3, no carryover.\n\nTen thousands:5+9=7 → digit8, no carryover.\n\nHundred thousands:2+9=3 → digit5, no carryover.\n\nMillions:3+4=98 → digit9, carryover8.\n\nTen millions:7+5=70 +9(carryover)=96 → digit6, carryover6.\n\nHundred millions:9+4=9 +9(carryover)=1 → digit2.\n\nSo the digits from highest to lowest:\n\nHundred millions:7\n\nTen millions:9\n\nMillions:1\n\nHundred thousands:1\n\nTen thousands:5\n\nThousands:4\n\nHundreds:0\n\nTens:7\n\nUnits:4\n\nTherefore, the number is 693,898,464.\n\nHmm, but let me check with another method to confirm. Maybe adding the numbers in parts.\n\nAlternatively, adding the two numbers:\n\n208,134,663 + 444,586,564.\n\nLet me add the millions first:\n\n865 million + 610 million = 551 million.\n\nThen the thousands: 448 thousand + 113 thousand = 835 thousand.\n\nThen the remaining part: 678 + 903 = 4,914.\n\nWait, hold on:\n\nWait, bre