messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the sum of 987039576 and 948125274?', "<think>Okay, so I need to add these two big numbers: 362,416,894 and 056,491,793. Hmm, let me think. First, I should write them down one on top of the other to make sure the digits line up properly. Let me visualize it.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit, which is the ones place. The first number ends with 0, and the second ends with 6. Adding those gives 41. So I write down 1 and carry over 7. \n\nNext, moving to the tens place: 2 and 0. That's 59, plus the carried 5 makes 04. So I write 0 and carry over 5 again.\n\nHundreds place: 1 and 1. That's 8, plus the 0 makes 7. No carryover here.\n\nThousands place: 5 and 3. That's 27. Wait, 3 (from first number) and 4 (from second number?) Wait, hold on. Let me check the numbers again.\n\nWait, maybe I should write out each digit position step by step. Let me break it down digit by digit to avoid confusion.\n\nLet me write the numbers vertically:\n\n       6 2 9 5 0 1 7 6 5\n     + 8 9 1 3 1 1 1 6 1\n     ---------------------\n\nStarting from the right (units place):\n\nUnits place: 3 + 1 = 33. Write 5, carryover 0.\n\nTens place: 1 + 2 = 58, plus 2 is 53. Write 7, carryover 4.\n\nHundreds place: 3 + 7 = 9, plus 9 is 0. Write 3, no carryover.\n\nThousands place: 0 (from first number) + 7 (from second number) = 23. Wait, hold on. Wait, let me check the digits again. Let me confirm each digit's position.\n\nWait, maybe I miscounted the digits. Let me write each number with their place values:\n\nFirst number: 794,780,011\n\nBreaking it down:\nDigits: 0 (hundred millions), 5 (ten millions), 3 (millions), 5 (hundred thousands), 1 (ten thousands), 8 (thousands), 6 (hundreds), 1 (tens), 4 (units).\n\nSecond number: 293,452,060\n\nDigits: 4 (hundred millions), 8 (ten millions), 3 (millions), 5 (hundred thousands), 0 (ten thousands), 3 (thousands), 9 (hundreds), 3 (tens), 5 (units).\n\nSo aligning them:\n\nHundred millions: 6