,5 (u)\n\nAdding each column:\n\nStarting from units (rightmost):\n\n1 +1 =64 → 3, carryover 2\n\nTens:4 +2 =25 +6=82 →4, carryover6\n\nHundreds:3+7=2+3=5 →3, no carryover\n\nThousands:1+6=98 →1, carryover2\n\nTen thousands:9+7=8 +8=2 →0\n\nHundred thousands:3+6=0 →6\n\nMillions:1+4=28 →1, carryover8\n\nTen millions:0+8=64 +5=21 →4, carryover6\n\nHundred millions:6+4=39 +8=98 →2, carryover6\n\nThen the final carryover 9 is added as a new digit at the billions place.\n\nSo putting all digits together from right to left:\n\nUnits:9\n\nTens:6\n\nHundreds:1\n\nThousands:2\n\nTen thousands:1\n\nHundred thousands:8\n\nMillions:6\n\nTen millions:6\n\nHundred millions:1\n\nBillions:6\n\nSo the total is 5,720,834,777.\n\nWait, let me confirm with another method. Maybe adding the numbers in parts.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using calculator-like addition step by step.\n\nAlternatively, adding the two numbers:\n\nFirst number: 603,101,438\n\nSecond number:173,843,421\n\nAdding them:\n\nLet me add the millions first:\n\n379,806,823 is 736 million plus 27,250.\n\n722,667,689 is 794 million plus 379,391.\n\nSo adding millions: 621,736,683 + 707,199,642 = 0,203,538,738.\n\nThen the remaining parts: 13,185 + 689,719 = ?\n\n70,348 + 346,360:\n\n24,043 + 844,095:\n\nAdding units:4+3=25, 5+2=68, 4+8=3, etc.\n\nAlternatively, 11,305 + 976,968:\n\n12,090\n\n+757,060\n\n= (47,248 + 858,656)\n\nLet me add them:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n8 +3=59 →6, carryover5\n\n0+2=26 +4=29 →3, carryover2\n\n4+1=8 +6=9 →3, carryover2\n\n5+2=32 →2, carryover3\n\n8 (ten thousands place) + 3 (ten thousands place?) Wait, let me write properly:\n\nWait, 70,882 is:\n\n6 (ten thousands), 5 (thousands), 9 (hundreds), 1 (tens), 0 (units).\n\n040,423 is:\n\n2 (hundred thousands), 3 (ten thousands), 9 (thousands), 8 (hundreds),8 (tens),8 (units).\n\nWait, actually, 550,043 is 5 (hundred thousands), 7 (ten thousands), 1 (thousands), 1 (hundreds), 4 (tens), 5 (units). So when adding to 72,638 (which is 4 (hundred thousands), 2 (ten thousands), 1 (thousands), 7 (hundreds), 8 (tens),1 (units)), we have to align properly.\n\nWait, perhaps I should write:\n\n   8 5 5 0 1 4\n\n+0 0 7 0 6 1\n\nBut that's not the right way. Let me do it step by step:\n\n98,289 + 318,946:\n\nAligning digits:\n\n      91,930\n\n    +809,387\n\n    ---------\n\nStarting from units:\n\n0 +3=28 →8, carryover2\n\n3+5=35 +8=88 →9, carryover2\n\n2+0=2 +9=0 →1, carryover1\n\n5 (thousands place) +2 (thousands place)=59 →7, carryover0\n\n6 (ten thousands place) +3 (ten thousands place)=3 +7=5 →1\n\n4 (hundred thousands place) →2\n\nSo total is 802,335.\n\nWait, let's see:\n\n11,240 +291,021:\n\n40,264 + 233,617 = 708,240\n\nThen add 61,016 more:\n\n550,980 +97,515 = 905,791? Wait, maybe my previous step was wrong.\n\nWait, 87,962 +716,939:\n\nLet me compute 96,352 + 913,199:\n\n98,684 + 764,318:\n\n91,924 + 677,802 = (78,115 + 569,219) + 67,850 = 044,208 +14,327 = 010,307. Yes, that matches the previous result.\n\nSo total of the two parts: 8,601,182,811 + 040,519 = 2,446,276,776.\n\nWait, but earlier when I did the digit by digit addition, I got 0,116,912,513. Hmm, there's a discrepancy here. Which one is correct?\n\nWait, let me check again.\n\nWait, in the first method, adding digit by digit, I had:\n\nAfter adding the millions and the smaller parts, but maybe I made an error in the digit-by-digit method.\n\nWait, in the first method:\n\nThe total digits were:\n\nBillions:4, Hundred millions:4, Ten millions:7, Millions:2, Hundred thousands:9, Ten thousands:7, Thousands:2, Hundreds:3, Tens:4, Units:1.\n\nWait, putting that together: 0,216,933,241.\n\nBut in the second method, adding the millions first gives 6,711,752,497 plus 389,404 gives 8,429,240,912. The difference is 5,896,330,928 vs 6,848,891,321. There's a difference of 9,417.\n\nHmm, so which is correct?\n\nLet me do the digit-by-digit addition again carefully:\n\nFirst number: 898,288,934\n\nSecond number:650,778,495\n\nLet me write them aligned:\n\n          3 5 3 6 2 1 1 8 8\n\n        + 4 5 5 9 6 9 5 1 2\n\n        ---------------------\n\nStarting from the right (units):\n\n0 +9 =79 →7, carryover3.\n\nTens:1+1=20 +7=72 →3, carryover9.\n\nHundreds:7+7=9 +8=1 →7, carryover7.\n\nThousands:1 (first number) +6 (second number) =69 →3, carryover4.\n\nTen thousands:6 +4=9 +5=5 →1, carryover4.\n\nHundred thousands:3 +9=5 →3, carryover8.\n\nMillions:1 +3=21 →4, carryover5.\n\nTen millions:7 +7=28 +3=80 →5, carryover0.\n\nHundred millions:7 +7=59 +3=83 →2, carryover2.\n\nBillions: carryover0 →0.\n\nSo the result is 8 (billions), 3 (hundred millions), 2 (ten millions), 8 (millions), 6 (hundred thousands), 5 (ten thousands), 5 (thousands), 5 (hundreds), 7 (tens), 6 (units).\n\nSo written out: 9,778,647,123.\n\nBut in the second method, when I broke it into millions and the rest:\n\n078,141,994 is 036,277,648 + 88,901\n\n784,759,597 is 526,817,647 + 270,153\n\nAdding the millions: 435,934,881 +036,885,736 = 4,261,891,827\n\nAdding the remaining parts: 72,102 +512,018 =387,745\n\nTotal sum: 9,797,386,663 +588,929 =5,727,808,673.\n\nWait, so there's a discrepancy of 7,633 between the two methods. Which one is correct?\n\nHmm, I must have messed up one of the calculations. Let me check the second method again.\n\nWait, 02,155 +316,990:\n\nLet me do 76,149 + 688,098 step by step:\n\n41,050 + 094,862 = 520,012\n\n022,624 + 33,639:\n\n13,346 +567,349:\n\nAdd 502,799 +92,464=663,682\n\n871,631 +8,343=939,497. Yes, that's correct.\n\nSo the total is 5,313,035,571.\n\nBut in the first method, digit by digit, I got 0,572,720,375. The difference is 5,435. Let's see where I went wrong.\n\nLooking at the digit-by-digit addition steps:\n\nThousands place: 5 (from first number) +0 (from second number)=90. So write 1, carryover8. That's correct.\n\nThen the ten thousands place:1 (first number) +1 (second number)=7 + carryover5=4. Correct.\n\nHundred thousands place:4 +5=8. Correct.\n\nMillions place:4 +3=52. So write 3, carryover0. Cor