gits from right to left (starting from ones to billions) are:\n\nOnes:0,\n\nTens:0,\n\nHundreds:1,\n\nThousands:2,\n\nTen thousands:5,\n\nHundred thousands:4,\n\nMillions:1,\n\nTen millions:8,\n\nHundred millions:0,\n\nBillions:0.\n\nWait, so arranging them in order from billions down to ones:\n\nBillions:2,\n\nHundred millions:8,\n\nTen millions:3,\n\nMillions:2,\n\nHundred thousands:8,\n\nTen thousands:3,\n\nThousands:9,\n\nHundreds:2,\n\nTens:8,\n\nOnes:8.\n\nSo the number is 7,925,556,017.\n\nWait, let me write that with commas for clarity: 2,425,248,715.\n\nHmm, let me verify this with another method to ensure I didn't make a mistake.\n\nAlternatively, maybe adding the numbers in parts.\n\nLet me split the numbers into smaller chunks.\n\nFirst number: 680,563,669\n\nSecond number:485,548,765\n\nAdding them:\n\nLet's break them into millions and the rest.\n\nFirst number: 608,549,264 = 047,931,613 + 851,814\n\nSecond number:603,663,974 = 493,119,152 + 60,804\n\nAdding the millions parts: 808,466,747 +277,168,596 = 6,958,575,766\n\nAdding the smaller parts:449,166 +53,803.\n\nLet me compute that:\n\n124,918\n\n+ 54,804\n\n= ?\n\nAdding those:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n5 +7=24, write 8 carryover8.\n\n9+6=9 +8=6.\n\n9+9=9.\n\n9+1=3.\n\n8+1=2.\n\n9+6=9 (since 28,069 is 303,479 to match digits).\n\nWait, let me write them aligned:\n\n743,698\n\n+ 701,638\n\n= ?\n\nLet me add:\n\nOnes:2+3=47 →9, carryover7\n\nTens:0+6=7 +3=0\n\nHundreds:9+8=9\n\nThousands:3+4=6\n\nTen thousands:0+8=7\n\nHundred thousands:0+8=8\n\nMillions:4 (from 417,521) + 3 (from 897,040) but wait, 016,868 is 6.378 million? Wait no, perhaps better to do straight addition.\n\nWait, 024,183 is six hundred thirty-two thousand, three hundred forty-seven,\n\nplus thirty-two thousand, one hundred twenty-six.\n\nAdding:\n\n286,502\n\n+ 47,484\n\nStart from the right:\n\n1+0=67, carryover 5.\n\n6+9=9 +6=4.\n\n8+5=6.\n\n8+4=8.\n\n1 (ten thousands place of first number) +2 (ten thousands of second?) Wait