o make sure I didn't skip any digits.\n\nStarting over:\n\nOnes place: 2 + 1 = 49. Record 5, carryover 0.\n\nTens: 4 +7 =22 +4=36. 8, carryover5.\n\nHundreds: 8 +2 =70 +0=30. 8, carryover2.\n\nThousands:6 +5 =4 +3=9. No carryover.\n\nTen thousands:5 +7=07. So 5, carryover3. Wait, here's a mistake. Wait, the ten thousands place: first number's digit is 8 (since the number is 444,521,724: breaking down, the digits from right: positions are ones (7), tens (3), hundreds (9), thousands (6), ten thousands (2), hundred thousands (1), millions (9), ten millions (6), hundred millions (2). So the ten thousands place is indeed the 2. The second number's ten thousands place is 9 (from 657,508,704: the digits are 2 (ones), 5 (tens), 3 (hundreds), 5 (thousands), 7 (ten thousands), 3 (hundred thousands), 6 (millions), 9 (ten millions), 6 (hundred millions). So yes, 8+3=94. So 3 in the ten thousands place, carryover 3.\n\nMoving to hundred thousands place: first number has 0, second has1. 2+2=35, plus the carryover 7 makes 98. So write 1, carryover0.\n\nMillions place: first number's millions digit is 0 (since after hundred thousands, millions is the next digit), second number's millions digit is 2. 6+9=2 plus 5 is 3. So 0, no carryover.\n\nTen millions place: first has 0, second has 6. 5+5=6.\n\nHundred millions place: 9 +0=2.\n\nPutting all together, the digits from right to left would be:\n\nStarting with the ones: 1 (from first step), then tens 6, hundreds 3, thousands 9, ten thousands 2, hundred thousands 5, millions 5, ten millions 6, hundred millions 1. Wait, but when written out, the total would be 1 (hundred millions), 6 (ten millions), 4 (millions), 5 (hundred thousands), 3 (ten thousands), 0 (thousands), 4 (hundreds), 6 (tens), 7 (ones). Wait, that can't be right because when adding 598,593,732 and 352,335,204, the sum should be over 036 million?\n\nWait, let's see. Let me add them in parts to check.\n\nFirst number: 856,159,525\n\nSecond number: 038,848,472\n\nAdding th