us the carryover 0 makes 25. So we have to write 6 and carryover 5 to the billions place.\n\nSo the total would be 8 (from the carryover) followed by 7, then the rest. Wait, let me put all the digits together:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes:3\n\nTens:6\n\nHundreds:5\n\nThousands:7\n\nTen thousands:2\n\nHundred thousands:9\n\nMillions:8\n\nTen millions:8\n\nHundred millions:9\n\nBillions:3 (carryover)\n\nSo putting them all together: 5 (billions), 5 (hundred millions), 9 (ten millions), 7 (millions), 9 (hundred thousands), 3 (ten thousands), 5 (thousands), 3 (hundreds), 7 (tens), 0 (ones). Wait, that can't be right. Let me check again.\n\nWait, when we get to the hundred millions place:\n\nHundred millions place: 7 + 8 = 36, plus the carryover from the ten millions place which was 0? Wait, let me retrace.\n\nWait, the ten millions place: first number has 7, second has 3. 4+7=38, so we write 6 and carryover 6. Then the hundred millions place: 4 +2 =65, plus the carryover 8 is 38. So that gives 9 in the hundred millions place and carryover 7 to the billions. So the billions place is 0.\n\nSo the total number is 3,9 (hundred millions), 1 (ten millions), 9 (millions), 3 (hundred thousands), 6 (ten thousands), 2 (thousands), 1 (hundreds), 7 (tens), 1 (ones). Wait, but the order should be:\n\nBillions digit first, then hundred millions, ten millions, etc. So putting it all together:\n\nBillions:4\n\nHundred millions:3\n\nTen millions:4\n\nMillions:0\n\nHundred thousands:0\n\nTen thousands:9\n\nThousands:4\n\nHundreds:8\n\nTens:9\n\nOnes:9\n\nSo combining these digits: 2,010,751,130? Let me see:\n\nBreaking down the number:\n\n3,698,439,470.\n\nWait, let me verify this addition another way to make sure. Maybe adding the numbers step by step.\n\nAlternatively, maybe adding the numbers in parts. Let's see:\n\nFirst number: 142,648,124\n\nSecond number: 215,396,971\n\nLet me add them digit by digit again carefully:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes: 1 + 5 = 9\n\nTens:8 