\nPositions:\n\n0 (units): 1 + 0 = 8\n\n7 (tens):3 +2 =7\n\n9 (hundreds):6 +8 =85 (write 6, carryover 8)\n\n1 (thousands):6 +2 =26 +9 (carry) =35 (write 8, carryover8)\n\n0 (ten thousands):0 +4 =3 +6 =5\n\n3 (hundred thousands):8 +9 =6\n\n0 (millions):7 +5 =68 (write 3, carryover2)\n\n6 (ten millions):3 +5 =6 +8 (carry) =5\n\n2 (hundred millions):8 +5 =4\n\nSo the total is 1 9 8 3 5 4 5 7 2?\n\nWait, let me structure it properly:\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit:\n\nPosition 2 (units): 5\n\nPosition 4 (tens):2\n\nPosition0 (hundreds):1\n\nPosition6 (thousands):2\n\nPosition6 (ten thousands):5\n\nPosition3 (hundred thousands):6\n\nPosition5 (millions):5\n\nPosition1 (ten millions):6\n\nPosition6 (hundred millions):4\n\nSo combining these digits from highest to lowest place:\n\nHundred millions:7, ten millions:8, millions:9, hundred thousands:6, ten thousands:2, thousands:6, hundreds:7, tens:2, units:0.\n\nSo the number is 933,860,553.\n\nWait, let me check again:\n\nWait, the digits in order from the highest place (hundred millions) to units:\n\n3 (hundred millions), 0 (ten millions), 3 (millions), 1 (hundred thousands), 9 (ten thousands), 2 (thousands), 1 (hundreds), 0 (tens), 6 (units). So that would be 911,262,376.\n\nHmm, but let me do a quick addition check using another method to confirm.\n\nAlternatively, maybe adding the numbers in parts. Let's see:\n\n480,566,618 + 865,259,789\n\nBreak it into 542,378,275 + 1,784,086 and 577,787,748 + 91,122,540\n\nAdding the millions first:\n\n513,847,545 + 956,266,911 = 497,968,955\n\nThen the remaining parts:\n\n4,605,163 + 92,651,293\n\nWait, 9,064,819 plus 06,819,147.\n\nAdding those:\n\n5,644,232 + 27,349,139\n\nLet me add 1 million +05 million =58 million.\n\nThen 453,363 +248,897 = 129,185.\n\nSo total would be 30,394,471 +134,331 =87,007,375.\n\nAdding that to the 138,991,974 gives 425,400,017. Okay, same result as before. That seems consistent.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use another check: subtract one number from