dding digit by digit again to confirm.\n\nLet me write down the numbers again with commas for clarity:\n\n424,994,443\n\n266,337,656\n\nAdding digit by digit from right:\n\nOnes: 1 + 5 = 98 → 6, carryover 3\n\nTens: 4 + 1 = 2 +0=0 → 2, no carryover\n\nHundreds:1 +7=31 →4, carryover4\n\nThousands:0+4=67 +8=50 →8, carryover7\n\nTen thousands:9+6=7 +0=3 →3\n\nHundred thousands:2 +0=63 →3, carryover3\n\nMillions:2+5=50 +5=24 →2, carryover6\n\nTen millions:8 +9=22 +3=73 →2, carryover7\n\nHundred millions:5 +6=4 +4=0 →6\n\nSo writing all the digits from right to left: 3,9,1,7,4,8,7,9,4 → 202,990,511. Yep, same result.\n\nHmm, so I think that's correct. Maybe I can also use a calculator to verify, but since I don't have one here, my manual checks all lead to the same answer, so I feel confident it's 035,196,354.\n\nWait, just to ensure I didn't misalign any digits. Let me check the positions again.\n\nFirst number: 1 (hundred millions), 6 (ten millions), 2 (millions), 2 (hundred thousands), 0 (ten thousands), 0 (thousands), 2 (hundreds), 9 (tens), 1 (ones).\n\nSecond number: 9 (hundred millions),5 (ten millions),6 (millions),2 (hundred thousands),2 (ten thousands),0 (thousands),8 (hundreds),0 (tens),7 (ones).\n\nYes, so when adding:\n\nHundred millions:6+5=4 plus carryover 3 makes 9. Correct.\n\nTen millions:9+5=47 plus carryover 3 makes 49. So digit 0, carryover3. Correct.\n\nMillions:3+3=90 plus carryover6 makes 24. So digit1, carryover6. Correct.\n\nHundred thousands:4+4=09 plus carryover7 makes 82? Wait, no, hold on. Wait, hundred thousands place: the first number's hundred thousands digit is 0 (since the number is 256,601,049: the digits are 0,5,9,0,3,3,8,5,5. The fourth digit from the right is thousands, so hundred thousands would be the fifth digit from the left? Wait, maybe I got the place values mixed up.\n\nWait, let me clarify the place values properly to ensure I didn't make a mistake in the digit positions.\n\nStarting from the right (units place):\n\nPosition