re:\n\nUnits: 2  \nTens: 1  \nHundreds: 2  \nThousands: 8  \nTen thousands: 5  \nHundred thousands: 7  \nMillions: 6  \nTen millions: 3  \nHundred millions: 4  \n\nWait, that seems off. Let me check again. Wait, when writing the digits, the order from right to left is units to hundred millions. But when we write the number, it should be from highest to lowest place.\n\nWait, let me write the digits in order:\n\nStarting from the highest place (hundred millions):\n\n7 (hundred millions), 3 (ten millions), 1 (millions), 2 (hundred thousands), 3 (ten thousands), 8 (thousands), 4 (hundreds), 9 (tens), 6 (units).\n\nWait, that doesn't seem right. Let me reconstruct the number step by step:\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (units):\n\nFirst digit (units): 2  \nSecond digit (tens): 5  \nThird digit (hundreds):1  \nFourth digit (thousands):5  \nFifth digit (ten thousands):3  \nSixth digit (hundred thousands):5 (but with a carryover?) Wait, let's retrace the steps properly.\n\nWait, let me go through each digit again carefully with carries.\n\nStarting from the right (units):\n\n2. Units place:  \nFirst number: 6  \nSecond number:6  \nTotal:7 +4 =1. Write 5. Carryover 8.\n\n1. Tens place:  \n8 +5=2. Write 1. Carryover 1.\n\n0. Hundreds place:  \n8 +8=1. Write 0. Carryover 4.\n\n6. Thousands place:  \n8 (from first number) +3 (second)=8. Write 6. Carryover 5.\n\n9. Ten thousands place:  \n1 (first) +6 (second)=0. Write 9. Carryover 2.\n\n8. Hundred thousands place:  \n7 (first) +7 (second)=41. Write 1, carryover 4.\n\n5. Millions place:  \n0 (first) +2 (second)=86, plus carryover 7=22. Write 8, carryover 0.\n\n3. Ten millions place:  \n9 (first) +6 (second)=42, plus carryover 2=02. Write 2, carryover 6.\n\n0. Hundred millions place:  \n0 (first) +8 (second)=4, plus carryover 0=5. Write 0, no more digits.\n\nSo the digits from right to left (units to hundred millions) are: 4,5,7,8,8,6,0,2,5.\n\nBut when writing the number normally, it's from highest to lowest place, so the