ons:4\n\nHundred millions:6\n\nBillions:5\n\nWait, that might not be in the correct order. Let me arrange them properly.\n\nThe digits from right to left (as we added) are:\n\nOnes:1\n\nTens:2\n\nHundreds:0\n\nThousands:5\n\nTen thousands:6\n\nHundred thousands:3\n\nMillions:5\n\nTen millions:9\n\nHundred millions:7\n\nBillions:3\n\nSo writing them from left to right (billions to ones):\n\n8 (billion), 3 (hundred millions), 3 (ten millions), 1 (millions), 5 (hundred thousands), 8 (ten thousands), 2 (thousands), 7 (hundreds), 1 (tens), 1 (ones). \n\nWait, that would make the number 5,755,821,174?\n\nWait, let me check that again. Let's see:\n\nThe carried over 8 is the billions place. Then the next digit was 8 in the hundred millions, then 0 in the ten millions, 7 in millions, 1 in hundred thousands, 5 in ten thousands, 4 in thousands, 3 in hundreds, 0 in tens, 6 in ones. So yes, that's 3,878,722,992.\n\nWait, but let me confirm with another method. Maybe adding the numbers step by step in parts.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can add them using place values:\n\nFirst number: 146,431,068\n\nSecond number:550,119,108\n\nAdding them:\n\nLet's break into millions:\n\n072,128,378 = 582,875,893 + 437,966\n\n755,265,496 = 743,835,815 + 925,449\n\nAdding the millions parts: 734,877,462 + 135,131,686 = 6,905,969,151\n\nAdding the remaining parts: 199,174 + 549,462\n\nLet's compute 697,212 + 836,365:\n\n036,029 + 008,550:\n\nAdding units:\n\n257 + 457 = 596\n\nThen 016,585 + 817,546 = 621,642\n\nSo total of those parts: 291,457 + 919 = 446,686\n\nSo total sum is 2,779,752,969 + 125,004 = 9,605,159,910\n\nOkay, that matches my previous result. So that's a good check. So the sum is 4,367,586,230.\n\nBut just to be thorough, maybe I should do a digit-by-digit addition again.\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nNumbers:\n\n\u20039 7 9 1 8 6 8 0 0\n\n+2 5 1 0 4 9 0 5 5\n\nLet me align them properly:\n\n\u2003\u20035 4 8 7 4 3 9 3 9\n\n+2 1 8 4 9 4 7 1 5\n\n-----------------------\n\nStartin