thousands)\n- 3 (thousands)\n- 5 (hundreds)\n- 2 (tens)\n- 0 (units)\n\nSecond number: 719,411,982 is also 4 digits:\n\n- 5 (hundred millions)\n- 3 (ten millions)\n- 2 (millions)\n- 5 (hundred thousands)\n- 7 (ten thousands)\n- 9 (thousands)\n- 9 (hundreds)\n- 4 (tens)\n- 0 (units)\n\nAdding each column:\n\nStarting from the right (units):\n\n7 + 8 = 2 → units:6\n\nTens:6 +7 =55 → write 3, carryover 8\n\nHundreds:1 +2 +8=4 → hundreds:7\n\nThousands:8 +4 =1 → thousands:3\n\nTen thousands:2 +5 =1 → ten thousands:5\n\nHundred thousands:0 +7 =50 → write 0, carryover 7\n\nMillions:5 +7 +2 (carryover)=0 → millions:9\n\nTen millions:9 +2 =3 → ten millions:5\n\nHundred millions:3 +5 =46 → write 5, carryover 8\n\nBillions: carryover 0 → billions:0\n\nSo putting all together, starting from billions down:\n\n9 (billions), 9 (hundred millions),0 (ten millions),7 (millions),6 (hundred thousands),2 (ten thousands),0 (thousands),1 (hundreds),4 (tens),3 (units). \n\nWait, but the thousands place was 0, so thousands digit is 4, but the hundreds is 5, tens is 4, units 5. \n\nWait, so the number is 5,725,231,504?\n\nWait, let me structure it properly with commas:\n\nBillions:9\n\nHundred millions:2 → so next is 71? Wait no, commas are placed every three digits starting from the right.\n\nWait, the number would be 2,899,727,293.\n\nBreaking it down:\n\n9 (billions),\n\n239 (hundred millions to millions? Wait, no, commas separate every three digits. Let me see:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nUnits: 7\n\nTens: 5 → 83\n\nHundreds:0 → 210\n\nThousands:1 → 4,015\n\nTen thousands:9 → 63,165\n\nHundred thousands:6 → 506,067\n\nMillions:0 → 8,737,899\n\nTen millions:4 → 97,601,434\n\nHundred millions:4 → 492,932,459 but since leading zeros are not written, it's 50,824,374 plus the 7 in the billions place.\n\nWait, so the total is 7,261,052,110.\n\nYes, that makes sense. Let me confirm by another method, maybe breaking the numbers into parts.\n\nAlternatively, let me add 423,863,825 + 242,572,9