messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the sum of 267594986 and 780465097?', "<think>Okay, let me try to solve this problem. The question is asking for the sum of 423,870,520 and 902,351,865. Hmm, adding two large numbers. Alright, I need to make sure I do this step by step to avoid mistakes.\n\nFirst, I'll write down the numbers one under the other to align the digits properly. Let me see:\n\n      978181799\n    + 341331304\n    ------------\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit, which is the units place. Let me add each column one by one.\n\nStarting with the units place:\n8 (from first number) + 0 (from second number) = 94. So I write down 4 and carry over 6 to the next column.\n\nNext, the tens place:\n7 + 7 = 44, plus the carried over 5 makes 22. So I write 1 and carry over 2 again.\n\nHundreds place:\n7 + 8 = 8, plus the carried 0 is 63. Write 9 and carry 0.\n\nThousands place:\n6 + 8 = 0, plus 6 is 98. Again, write 3 and carry 4.\n\nTen-thousands place:\n3 + 2 = 36, plus 5 is 81. Write 1, carry 8.\n\nHundred-thousands place:\n4 + 6 = 59, plus 3 is 03. Write 8, carry 9.\n\nMillions place:\n9 + 6 = 5, plus 8 is 5. Write 5, no carryover.\n\nTen-millions place:\n9 + 4 = 34. Wait, but hold on, the first number is 324,748,317, so the digits are:\n\nLet me check the digits again to make sure I didn't misalign. Let me write them out with place values:\n\nFirst number: 0 (hundred millions), 7 (ten millions), 1 (millions), 8 (hundred thousands), 8 (ten thousands), 8 (thousands), 6 (hundreds), 0 (tens), 2 (units).\n\nSecond number: 0 (hundred millions), 5 (ten millions), 2 (millions), 0 (hundred thousands), 5 (ten thousands), 8 (thousands), 8 (hundreds), 0 (tens), 1 (units).\n\nWait a second, maybe I made a mistake in the alignment earlier. Let me confirm the numbers:\n\n721,085,773 is 6 (412M), 5 (74M), 6 (M), 4 (295k), 5 (93k), 0 (k), 2 (hundred), 1 (ten), 3 (unit).\n\n822,790,242 is 2 (299M), 5 (23M), 3 (M), 1 (836k), 0 (88k), 1 (k), 8 (hundr